.el .ds Aq '
.TH dohsub 1  "dohsub 0.1.1"
.SH NAME
dohsub \- Serve a local QX subscription with automatically updated DoH\-resolved IPv4 addresses.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdohsub\fR [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve a local QX subscription with automatically updated DoH\-resolved IPv4 addresses.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and repository (no network)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
dohsub\-config(1)
Save or inspect private cached settings; changes apply on next start/restart
.TP
dohsub\-start(1)
Validate DoH, reserve a loopback port and start the background subscription service
.TP
dohsub\-import(1)
Stage nodes from a private QX text, ss:// or servers JSON file
.TP
dohsub\-add(1)
Import node configuration from the local clipboard
.TP
dohsub\-restart(1)
Stop then start using cached configuration; validates DoH before stopping
.TP
dohsub\-stop(1)
Stop the managed dohsub daemon
.TP
dohsub\-list(1)
List staged nodes and active publication status without passwords
.TP
dohsub\-refresh(1)
Load staged nodes and queue one immediate DNS refresh, bypassing backoff once
.TP
dohsub\-remove(1)
Remove one node by exact tag, with a one\-level backup; reload if running
.TP
dohsub\-copy\-resource(1)
Copy the private QX server_remote subscription line to the clipboard
.TP
dohsub\-restore(1)
Restore the node snapshot from before the latest modification; reload if running
.TP
dohsub\-version(1)
Print exactly two lines: version and repository URL
.TP
dohsub\-upgrade(1)
Check GitHub releases and optionally upgrade the owning installation
.TP
dohsub\-completion(1)
Generate shell completion without reading or writing configuration
.TP
dohsub\-man(1)
Write the man page to stdout without initializing state
.TP
dohsub\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  dohsub config set \-\-doh https://dns.example.com/dns\-query
  dohsub import \-\-file ~/Downloads/nodes.txt
  dohsub start
  dohsub copy\-resource

macOS and Linux. curl is required for HTTPS. State: ~/.dohsub (private).
.SH VERSION
v0.1.1
.SH DESCRIPTION
The resident service binds only to 127.0.0.1. It resolves unique node hostnames using
HTTPS GET with an RFC 8484 DNS wire query, then publishes QX Shadowsocks nodes with
public IPv4 addresses. It does not route traffic or change system DNS.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
chmod 600 ~/Downloads/nodes.txt
dohsub config set --doh https://dns.example.com/dns-query
dohsub import --file ~/Downloads/nodes.txt
dohsub start
dohsub copy-resource
dohsub config --list
dohsub refresh
dohsub stop
.fi
Paste the copied line into QX [server_remote] and refresh in QX.
Use "dohsub help COMMAND" for options and examples, including nested "config set".
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: success or cancelled upgrade. 1: operation failed, including partial import
(accepted nodes remain saved). 2: command-line syntax error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
DOHSUB_HOME overrides ~/.dohsub for all private state. NO_COLOR disables colored
import indicators. HOME supplies the default state and installer prefix.
.SH FILES
~/.dohsub/config.json: cached DoH URL, port and optional interface.
.br
~/.dohsub/nodes.json: staged nodes. nodes.previous.json: one-step backup.
.br
~/.dohsub/runtime.json: active snapshot. dns-cache.json: TTL cache and retry state.
.br
~/.dohsub/token: subscription access token. control.sock: private local IPC.
.br
The directory is mode 700; private files are mode 600. Node input files must also
be regular files owned by the user with mode 600.
.SH CAVEATS
The upgrade command checks stable GitHub releases; --yes authorizes an
available upgrade.
The daemon is manually started and does not enable login startup.
.br
Successful import validates syntax; publication requires a public IPv4 and does
not verify the Shadowsocks handshake or reachability of the proxy port.
.br
New imports are staged until confirmed (y/yes), imported with -y, or loaded by
refresh/restart. Default confirmation is no, including EOF and noninteractive use.
.br
DNS successes honor TTL (5 seconds to 1 hour). Negative answers retry from 15
minutes to 6 hours; network failures from 30 seconds to 15 minutes, with jitter.
Stale resolved addresses can be published for at most 15 minutes after expiry.
No resolved nodes produces HTTP 503; QX should retain its existing subscription.
.br
Default/cached occupied ports increment; an explicit --port collision fails.
Protect the printed subscription URL and clipboard contents: they authorize
reading node credentials. The token is not printed by list or diagnostics.
.SH SEE ALSO
curl(1), ssh(1)
